    Thumbnail="http://data1.wwtassets.org/feeds/jwst/potm2409b/thumb.jpg"
    ZoomLevel="0.978994240745445"
  >
    <Description>The open cluster Westerlund 1 is located roughly 12 000 light-years away in the southern constellation Ara (the Altar) where it resides behind a huge interstellar cloud of gas and dust. It is an incomparable natural laboratory for the study of extreme stellar physics, helping astronomers to find out how the most massive stars in our Galaxy live and die. The unique draw of Westerlund 1 is its large, dense, and diverse population of massive stars, which has no counterpart in other known Milky Way galaxy clusters in terms of the number of stars and the richness of spectral types and evolutionary phases.</Description>
    <ForegroundImageSet>
